# seed: 2
# requires: hero_ready spell_learn spell_cast music_play
# requires-match: spell_cast caster=hero
# requires-match: spell_cast caster=monster
#
# STATUS: spell_learn and `spell_cast caster=hero` are both produced and verified on this
# binary. `spell_cast caster=monster` is NOT reachable from a level-1 hero in retail
# Evergreen; the evidence is at the bottom of this header. The requires line is left
# exactly as inherited - do not weaken it.
#
# THE ROUTE
#   Pick-a-Soul -> class 7 "Book-User" -> the Gateway of Dreams (map 0 link 0, scene 3,
#   answer the golden-rule `ASK 30` with `key y`, buy nothing, leave) -> the random
#   encounter the walk out triggers -> map 0 link 9 "Macgyver Castle" (151,275) -> map 2
#   link 12 "Hand Training" (QuestScenes200.txt:1173, SCENE 290).
#
# WHY CLASS 7. PP is paid at battle.c:1270, `hero_add_pp(hero, WIS*200/255+5)`, once per
# committed hero action. Every class's `START_ABILITY` in levels.txt was read: the maximum
# starting WIS in the whole world is 10, and only three classes have it. Class 7 pays
# 10*200/255+5 = 12 PP an action against class 1 Sword-User's WIS 0 -> 5. Cheapest
# learnable spell is 250 PP (see PP FLOOR), so 21 actions instead of 50.
# The six `key DOWN` presses are in the Pick-a-Soul panel (front.c:855-857,
# `selected_class`), not on the map: `EVT new_soul_created name=SpellStudent class=7`.
#
# PP FLOOR. FUN_0047FCED (world.c:642 complete_spells) seeds pp at 5000 and grows it 1.5x
# per required-affinity level, then FUN_0047FCF7 divides by 20, so the cheapest spell in
# Evergreen is 5000/20 = 250 PP. spells.txt gives no spell an explicit price: the ppCost
# column is 0 (=auto) on every learnable row. Only nine spells are learnable at
# element-affinity 0, and the first is spell 1 "Dirt" (element 3); spell 201 "Health
# Weave" (element 0) is index 7 of the nine. Both cost exactly 250 PP.
# No scene in the world does `GIVE P<n>` - `grep -rhoE "GIVE [A-Z][0-9]+"` over every
# extracted/worlds/Evergreen script returns no P at all - so the only scripted PP is
# missions.ini RewardPP, and the only affordable mission ([1] Jelly Bellies, 1000 PP) needs
# 5x trophy 1 at a 5 % drop.
#
# THE PP FARM IS SCENE 290's OWN LOSS LOOP, and it is deterministic:
#     @3 MOVE 1,45,75 / FIGHT 1, 4 / IF ALIVE, @4
#     on a loss six `'` lines / GIVE L1 / GIVE H5000 / GIVE M5000 / GOTO @3
# `L` is the resurrect opcode (scene.c:746), so the loop re-enters the same two-monster
# fight (Green Jelly id 1 + Flesh Crab id 4) forever with no walking. hero_died()
# (battle.c:709) halves only the XP progress, never the PP wallet, so the PP accumulates:
# measured 12 PP per committed hero action, 384 PP after 18 iterations of the loop.
#
# LEARN, THEN CAST.
#   * `click 358 32` is button_rect(5) = {640-48-3-51*5, 8, 48, 48} = (334,8,48,48), the
#     Spell slot (scene.c:1384). The scene VM is suspended while a panel is active
#     (scene.c:1367), so the click lands mid-dialogue and does not also advance the script.
#   * Seven `key DOWN` walk the selection to index 7 = spell 201 "Health Weave", then `l`
#     (panels.c:426-431) calls hero_learn_spell. `EVT spell_learn spell=201 pp=134`
#     (384 - 250 = 134).
#   * `key s` opens the in-fight spell chooser (battle.c:1605), `2` picks slot 1, RETURN
#     confirms (battle.c:1473), `a` commits: `EVT spell_cast caster=hero spell=201
#     target=0 dmg=-50`.
#   * Health Weave rather than Dirt is deliberate, and it is not a workaround for a port
#     bug. FUN_004904EB (battle.c:1212) is the original's pre-cast fizzle: it is DEX of
#     the TARGET minus DEX of the CASTER, and a positive difference fizzes at that many
#     per cent. Class 7 starts with DEX 0, every monster derives at least level*175/100
#     DEX, so an attack spell aimed at a monster always fizzles and logs nothing - the
#     early `if (fight.fizzle) return;` at battle.c:1106 is silent. A heal has no enemy
#     to aim at: spell_target() picks the caster's own slot, the DEX difference is exactly
#     0, and the cast-success roll at battle.c:1172 is gated on `element > 0`. So a heal
#     is the spell a WIS-10/DEX-0 class can actually land.
#
# WHY `spell_cast caster=monster` IS NOT REACHABLE HERE.
# monsters.txt arg 20 (the optional pet AI string) is empty in all 163 rows - that part is
# true - but it is not the column that gates monster spellcasting. monsters.txt:277-289
# documents arg 16 `wisdom` as the cast gate ("0 = Monster has NO wisdom and casts NO
# spells.. EVER", "-1 = by algorithm (based on level)"), and FUN_0048e810's ring walk
# (battle.c:948-976) selects from arg 16 alone. Column census of all 163 monster rows:
# 21 have wisdom 0, 136 have wisdom -1, 4 have wisdom 255 (ids 2000-2003, the level-80
# Element Masters); monsters.txt:524 (id 211 "Tri Wyrm") is short a column and its
# arg-16 slot holds "growl2.wav".
# Two independent walls stop a level-1 hero from ever seeing a caster:
#   1. Reachability. Every monster this replay can meet is id 1-4 - Green Jelly, Archer
#      Fish, Archer Fish, Flesh Crab - and all four have wisdom 0. Measured over 40 seeds
#      (1..40), the random encounter triggered by walking out of the Gateway only ever
#      rolls ids 1-3. SCENE 290's `@1 FIGHT 1` and `@3 FIGHT 1, 4` use ids 1 and 4. The
#      first fight in the world a level-1 hero could reach that contains a caster-capable
#      monster is SCENE 290's `@5 FIGHT 5` (Slobber, id 5, wisdom -1), and @5 is gated
#      behind WINNING `@3 FIGHT 1, 4` - the Flesh Crab hits for 22 and a fresh Book-User
#      has 20 max HP, so that branch is unreachable.
#   2. Frequency. FUN_0048e810's closing gate (battle.c:970-976) cancels a monster's
#      chosen spell unless `rand()%500 < wisdom` AND `rand()%1000 < wisdom`. Slobber is
#      level 4, so `derived(-1, 4, 231, 100)` gives it wisdom 9, and both gates pass
#      together 9/500 * 9/1000 = 0.016 % of the time. Only the wisdom-255 Element Masters
#      (245/500 * 745/1000 = 36 %) cast at a rate a replay can rely on, and they are
#      level-80 bosses.
